# Design refinement — canonical predicate for "current response affected"

## `BannerEmissionContext::affected_by(signal) -> bool`

Single source of truth for the "did this signal affect the current response" decision. Each operation builds a context and consults it:

```rust
pub struct BannerEmissionContext {
    operation: OperationKind,         // search | context | remember | ...
    fallbacks_taken: Vec<FallbackKind>,
    requested_features: Vec<FeatureKind>,
}

impl BannerEmissionContext {
    pub fn affected_by(&self, signal: DegradedCode) -> bool {
        match (self.operation, signal) {
            (OperationKind::Search, DegradedCode::SearchIndexStale) => {
                // affected if the response actually fell back to the older index
                self.fallbacks_taken.contains(&FallbackKind::StaleIndexFallback)
            }
            (OperationKind::Context, DegradedCode::GraphSnapshotUnimplemented) => false,
            // graph snapshot unimplemented does NOT affect context unless graph was requested
            (OperationKind::Context, DegradedCode::PackProfileBudgetCapped) => {
                self.requested_features.contains(&FeatureKind::PackBudgetOverride)
            }
            // ... full table of (operation, signal) → bool
        }
    }
}
```

A `(operation, signal)` lookup table lives in `src/diag/affected_table.rs` and is exhaustively tested.

## Banner emission rule

```rust
pub fn emit_advisory_banner(ctx: &BannerEmissionContext) -> Option<AdvisoryBanner> {
    let affected: Vec<_> = ctx.signals.iter()
        .filter(|s| ctx.affected_by(*s))
        .collect();
    if affected.is_empty() { None } else { Some(AdvisoryBanner::from(affected)) }
}
```

## Diagnostic verbose mode

Flag `--include-non-affecting-degradations` returns the full signal list (current behavior). Off by default. Used by `ee diag` workflows.

## Test plan addition

`tests/banner_emission_exhaustive.rs` table-driven test:
- For every `(OperationKind, DegradedCode)` pair, assert the affected_by decision matches the canonical table
- For every actual operation in `scripts/e2e_overhaul/diagnostics_honesty.sh`, assert banner emission matches `affected_by` decisions
- Fails CI if a new degraded code is added without an `affected_by` entry

## Migration

Existing call sites that emit banners unconditionally get refactored to construct `BannerEmissionContext` and call `emit_advisory_banner()`. The signal categorization table from the description (build_time / workspace_state / runtime) lives in `affected_table.rs` as data.

